 * acme-rules — Dynamic Rule Engine
 *
 * POST /check  evaluates a declarative rule against a caller-supplied context.
 *
 * NOTE ON THE REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION IN docs/RULES_ENGINE.md
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The reference uses `new Function(...)` to execute a caller-supplied string
 * as JavaScript.  That is Remote Code Execution (RCE): any client can read
 * files, spawn processes, or crash the server.  It has been intentionally
 * replaced with the safe declarative evaluator below.
