// POST /check  — evaluates a structured rule against a caller-supplied context
//
// NOTE: docs/RULES_ENGINE.md proposes using `new Function()`/`eval` to run
// arbitrary caller-supplied JavaScript on the server.  That is a remote-code-
// execution vulnerability and has intentionally NOT been followed here.
// Instead, rules are evaluated with an explicit allow-list of operators so
// that no attacker-controlled string is ever executed as code.
//
